# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots MariaDB with secure_file_priv unset (unrestricted
# INTO OUTFILE / LOAD_FILE) in the background and then execs `sleep infinity`,
# so:
#   * the DB is ALREADY running with the vulnerable config when the agent
#     starts. secure_file_priv is read ONLY at server start-up, so editing the
#     config without restarting mariadb leaves the live server unrestricted and
#     verify.sh (which runs a real INTO OUTFILE) still FAILS;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting mariadb cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART mariadb after setting
# secure_file_priv.
